2
H
+
. Higher temperatures in Orion B may also lead to elevated 
12
CO intensities.






The shape of the PDF can also change the intensity relationship. We employed the log-normal or a combination of log-normal and power-law PDFs. If the actual PDFs significantly differ from these ones, the N
2
H
+
-HCN relationship will have different slopes. For example, if the beam contains regions that are almost void of gas (i.e., a beam filling factor of less than unity), the PDFs will have double peaks. In this case, the points in Figure 
6
 shift downwards and leftward along lines with slopes of 1.






