2610.19701v1,Runtime Monitoring of Supermartingale Certificates,We aim to address the following research questions.,"6 
Conclusion




We introduced the first framework for runtime monitoring of supermartingale certificates for temporal properties that is applicable to both discrete- and continuous-time systems and to a broad range of supermartingale certificates. Our framework bounds the probability of ever raising a false alarm by a given threshold. Experimental evaluation demonstrates the practical effectiveness of our method for detecting supermartingale certificate violations at runtime in a range of stochastic control tasks. Interesting directions of future work include designing shielding and repair procedures that would use the alarms raised by our runtime monitoring framework.








AI use statement




We used ChatGPT to assist with writing, literature search, theoretical development, and the design and implementation of experiments. We describe these uses below. For writing, we used these tools to draft and revise text, simplify explanations, shorten sections, and improve consistency in notation and terminology. We also used them to assist with LaTeX formatting, e.g., constructing tables. For literature search, we used these tools to identify relevant work and compare its assumptions and guarantees with ours. For theoretical development, we used these tools to suggest proof arguments, expand derivations, and identify possible gaps and counterexamples. They also helped clarify certain measure-theoretic arguments required in the continuous-time setting. For experiments, we used these tools to write basic code and generate plots. They supported the selection of system disturbances. They were used to draft the experimental setup in the appendix.
The authors take full responsibility for the final content of the paper, including all AI-assisted text, mathematical claims and proofs, references, code, and experimental results.",cues
