In this paper, we proposed the SEED-MAX and SEED-MAX-F-Test feature selection methods for pruning redundant features generated by W-RKS. We derived a lower bound for the probability of correct feature selection by SEED-MAX and demonstrated theoretically that this bound can be made arbitrarily close to 1, albeit at the expense of increasing the training data size. Empirical evaluations conducted on UCR datasets showed that the SEED-MAX method, when combined with F-Test post-processing, achieved approximately 92% feature pruning with less than 1% degradation in classification accuracy. The rate of pruning advantage of our proposed methods becomes especially evident in multi-class classification problems involving many classes, where SEED-MAX-F-Test demonstrates superior performance compared to state-of-the-art approaches.",cues
