An analytical difficulty arises from our admissible curves being merely absolutely continuous and lying in a possibly nonsmooth subset of the Wasserstein space for which classical tangent spaces are unavailable. We overcame this difficulty by proving an almost-everywhere Euler approximation using the superposition principle for the continuity equation and the Banach-valued Lebesgue differentiation theorem, thereby obtaining the pointwise formulation of the IWCC in terms of Wasserstein contingent cones.






