Problem 1
.","6 
Conclusion




This work presents a Markov Jump system framework for robust NRHO stationkeeping under statistical missed thrust events, maneuver execution errors, and linearization errors. We model missed thrust events as a Markov chain fitted to exponential distribution-based failure and recovery statistics, and utilize bounded multiplicative noise to model maneuver execution error and linearization errors. We then study the corresponding
linear time-varying periodic Markov jump system with multiplicative noise and propose an LMI-based controller synthesis framework that respects path constraints with probability one. To enforce path constraints, we introduce the notion of a 
T
T
-periodic robust positively invariant sequence of sets, and combine it with Lyapunov-like stability constraints in the synthesis framework. We demonstrate the robustness of our framework through numerical results on the Earth-Moon 9:2 NRHO and a Saturn-Enceladus 
L
1
L_{1}
 NRHO stationkeeping example. For the impulsive propulsion case, we propose a three-mode MJLS structure, which provides contingency maneuver locations that are activated only when an MTE causes a planned burn to be missed. Further parametric study also offers insight into the characteristics of the MTE-resilient solution and its dependence on various problem parameters. Our framework enables robust maneuver planning for stationkeeping that is resilient against an arbitrary number of missed thrust events, maneuver execution errors, and linearization errors through the multiplicative noise-based Markov Jump System framework.








