2610.10909v1,Power Side-Channel Membership Inference Attack on Embedded Machine Learning,"Rather, they arise from a sequence of data-dependent computations that modulate the instantaneous power consumption of the processor. We hypothesize that power traces collected during inference can retain membership-dependent information correlated with the internal computations that determine the model output, even when detailed model outputs are unavailable to the adversary. The top panel shows that the selected model exhibits
