The HybridMC framework provides a fast detailed Monte Carlo simulation of optical calorimeters by decoupling the high-energy shower development, handled by Geant4, from the optical photon transport, reproduced via a parametrised summary Monte Carlo step driven by probability density functions extracted from a one-time full ray-tracing optical calibration. A Monte Carlo-to-Monte Carlo validation has shown statistical equivalence of the output with full ray-tracing, with the Kolmogorov-Smirnov test confirming good agreement for more than 
