-estimation with a monotone operator, we constructed a distribution-free estimating equation and then solved for its root via a computationally efficient stochastic approximation procedure. Our results show that estimation is possible at a parametric rate without modeling or estimating the covariate distribution. Moreover, the matching lower bounds that we derive also show that the nonstandard dependence of our upper bounds on the missingness probability is intrinsic to the problem. The key takeaway is that missingness in covariates can impose a substantially more intricate statistical cost in logistic regression than in the extensively studied linear regression problem. We conclude by discussing a few natural open directions.






