\ell
BISG probabilities as its first-stage estimates and then uses the surname as a proxy predictive of race, while assuming that the surname is independent of the outcome conditional on race and geography. Although the BIRDiE assumption may not hold perfectly, it corrects the attenuation bias of other standard downstream estimation approaches that assume conditional independence between race and outcome conditional on name and geography.
