Here we have demonstrated that a ResNet-Inspired Conditional VAE is able to accurately emulate the stochastic metastable Holton-Mass model of sudden stratospheric warmings. Although we trained only on one-day predictions, the emulator is able to match both short-term and long-term statistics, including the two-dimensional structure of important variables such as the state PDF, transition committor function, and transition expected lead time. Moreover, a PCA analysis of the Emulator’s latent space reveals four clusters associated with the two metastable states and the two transition pathways. This work serves as a promising demonstration of an effective analysis method to build an interpretable emulator of a stochastic climate model for subseasonal to seasonal forecasting and extreme event early warning.








