In this work, we introduced a novel method, WOLF, for robustly solving multi-agent motion planning problems over long time horizons. Leveraging previous work in robust single agent motion planning, tube model predictive control techniques are extended to multi-agent systems via a game-theoretic formulation. This direction included developing a sufficient condition for robust constraint tightening for generalized multi-agent constraints. The numerical effectiveness of this method was demonstrated via an on-orbit jamming game and a sun-blocking game. The WOLF algorithm extends the capabilities of differential game solvers to be robust to disturbances while solving competitive game scenarios.








